Z||000000||3fifty||07-19-2001||09:47 PM||||I have a 85 GT 2.8 with no reading on the temp gauge. Page 125 of the Haynes manual says that some vehicles have an optional temp gauge that reads between 100 and 260 degrees and that if it has the gauge that a transducer rather than a coolant temp switch is used. I thought all Fieros had a temp gauge in the cluster. Which should I have, the coolant temp switch or a transducer?<BR>Thanks, 3fifty one day!!!!!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fierokid87||07-20-2001||03:26 AM||||As far as i know there always has been a temp gauge.  The 84, though had a volt meter where the oil presure guage is on the 85-88 4 cyld.<P>Scott<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="BLOODY"> Fierokid's  Web site <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero</A> <P>AIM: Fierokid87<BR>ICQ: Fierokid</FONT><P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sfiero.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by Fierokid87 (edited 07-20-2001).]||||reg||4
